+# Danus architecture on OpenCode
+
+Danus keeps its mathematical state and orchestration engine independent from the
+model runtime. This adaptation uses OpenCode for every agent call.
+
+```text
+OpenCode Desktop main session
+  ├─ Danus MCP                 project memory, facts, literature tools
+  ├─ write-paper MCP           paper assembly and verification
+  ├─ human-summary MCP         progress reports
+  └─ Danus loop plugin         recurring work in the same session
+
+Danus project
+  ├─ main agent                strategy and dispatch
+  ├─ OpenCode worker sessions  proof search and fact submission
+  ├─ OpenCode verifier         fresh judgment for each submitted claim
+  ├─ global memory             findings, dead ends, elaborations, guidance
+  └─ fact graph                verifier-accepted mathematical claims
+```
 
-Danus turns the Rethlas single-problem proof engine (a codex agent plus proving
-skills, inherited rather than redesigned) into a multi-agent, long-running,
-strategy-steered research system, and renders verified results into papers and
-human progress reports. This is the as-built map: the layered model, the folder
-layout, the invariants, and the pinned cross-module contracts.
+## Boundaries
 
-For the main agent's operating contract, see `AGENTS.md`
-(→ `agents/contracts/main_agent.md`).
+The main agent manages projects and writes strategic guidance. Its MCP role has
+no `fact_submit` tool. Workers can submit claims and can add findings. The
+verifier can read literature tools and writes its decision file. A claim reaches
+the fact graph after the gateway receives a `correct` verifier decision.
 
----
+Project state lives under `runtime/projects/<project>/`. Each worker has a local
+home with `AGENTS.md`, `.agents/skills`, `TASK.md`, local memory, logs, and an
+`opencode.json` that pins the worker's Danus MCP role and project path.
 
