+Worker status records the last OpenCode session id, model, tokens, and reported
+cost. The strategy envelope carries the same usage fields. Provider pricing
+metadata determines whether OpenCode can report a dollar amount.
+
+## Main-session scheduling
+
+`.opencode/plugins/danus-loop.ts` supplies four tools:
+
+- `danus_loop_create` creates a fixed recurring prompt;
+- `danus_loop_list` lists jobs owned by the current session;
+- `danus_loop_delete` removes jobs from the current session;
+- `danus_schedule_wakeup` schedules an adaptive wakeup one to sixty minutes away.
+
+The scheduler checks due jobs once per second. A busy session marks the job
+pending and receives one prompt after it becomes idle. Several missed periods
+are combined. Jobs persist in `runtime/opencode-loops.json`, expire after seven
+days, and fixed jobs remain attached to their OpenCode session. Danus maintains
+one adaptive main-agent wakeup per checkout; a later conversation takes ownership
+when it schedules the next review. Adaptive wakeups receive one twenty-minute
+fallback opportunity when the agent omits its next schedule.
+
+## Configuration
+
+The root `opencode.json` registers the main MCP services. Worker and verifier
+configurations are generated beside their `AGENTS.md` files. Provider credentials
+stay in OpenCode. Danus-specific model and variant selections live in the
+gitignored `config/danus.env`.
+
+## Services
+
+The verifier is a local HTTP service at `127.0.0.1:8091`. The optional dashboard
+uses `127.0.0.1:8099`. `scripts/services.sh` owns their process lifecycle and
+records which services should return after host recovery.
 
